window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b335-3bdf97f87eea2d75.json"]={sha256:"3bdf97f87eea2d75f031a82fc9875f53342183a68fd0314d0b36cdc6c2da2b35",value:{"id":"b335","title":"鹿特丹港貝圖威貨運線","titleEn":"Betuweroute freight railway","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"鹿特丹港貝圖威貨運線以「港區貨運列車的阻力制動與容量協同」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。專用貨運線把港區裝卸、列車編組與幹線運行連成同一條物流鏈，列車較長與較重會同時改變加速、制動及站場占用，單看最高速度不足以推估吞吐量。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops coordinating freight resistance braking and port capacity through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. A dedicated freight line links port handling, train assembly and mainline movement; longer heavier trains change acceleration, braking and yard occupation together, so maximum speed alone does not determine throughput. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-integration","subcategoryTitle":"車站機廠與系統整合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Stations depots and integration","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-integration","learningTags":["rail","rail-integration","rail"],"architectureFamily":"rail-system","architectureNodes":[["港區裝卸","Port handling"],["貨列編組","Freight consist"],["路線牽引","Route traction"],["閉塞容量","Block capacity"],["港區周轉","Port turnover"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-system","labels":["港區裝卸","貨列編組","路線牽引","閉塞容量","港區周轉"],"labelsEn":["Port handling","Freight consist","Route traction","Block capacity","Port turnover"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n=5 trains/h, q=1800 t/train；y=n*q=9000 t/h。只把 n 增加百分之十，y=9900 t/h。模型邊界：固定每列有效載重與發車率，不含尖峰到達或空車需求；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=2000000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, s=0.01 1；y=m*g*s/1000=196.2 kN。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=215.82 kN。模型邊界：全列車處於同一小坡度，只計重力沿軌分量；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: n=5 trains/h, q=1800 t/train; y=n*q=9000 t/h. Increasing only n with a ten-percent increase gives y=9900 t/h. Boundary: Fixed useful payload and departure rate, excluding peak arrivals and empty returns; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=2000000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, s=0.01 1; y=m*g*s/1000=196.2 kN. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=215.82 kN. Boundary: The whole consist occupies one small gradient; only longitudinal gravity is included; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b335-v16-s1","title":"列車單向運能與坡道牽引分力","titleEn":"Directional train throughput & Gradient traction force","description":"本階段聚焦「列車單向運能」與「坡道牽引分力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Directional train throughput\" and \"Gradient traction force\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b335-v16-01","title":"列車單向運能：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Directional train throughput: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「列車單向運能」如何影響鹿特丹港貝圖威貨運線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Directional train throughput” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Betuweroute freight railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"運能是班次與有效載重的乘積，空車回送及車站衝突仍會消耗路徑。本模型把 n 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 9900 t/h。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。固定每列有效載重與發車率，不含尖峰到達或空車需求。使用滿載率與實際發車間距作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「列車單向運能」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Throughput multiplies departures by useful payload, while empty returns and conflicting moves still consume paths. In this model, n is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 9900 t/h. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Fixed useful payload and departure rate, excluding peak arrivals and empty returns. Use load factor and actual departure intervals as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Directional train throughput” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n=5 trains/h, q=1800 t/train；y=n*q=9000 t/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: n=5 trains/h, q=1800 t/train; y=n*q=9000 t/h.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「列車單向運能」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Directional train throughput”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-01-k1","title":"列車單向運能","titleEn":"Directional train throughput","text":"運能是班次與有效載重的乘積，空車回送及車站衝突仍會消耗路徑。本模型把 n 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 9900 t/h。","textEn":"Throughput multiplies departures by useful payload, while empty returns and conflicting moves still consume paths. In this model, n is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「列車單向運能」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Directional train throughput\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量","運能是班次與有效載重的乘積，空車回送及車站衝突仍會消耗路徑。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow.","Throughput multiplies departures by useful payload, while empty returns and conflicting moves still consume paths.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force."],"answer":1,"explanation":"運能是班次與有效載重的乘積，空車回送及車站衝突仍會消耗路徑。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Throughput multiplies departures by useful payload, while empty returns and conflicting moves still consume paths. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b335-v16-02","title":"列車單向運能：定量估算","titleEn":"Directional train throughput: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「列車單向運能」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Directional train throughput” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n=5 trains/h, q=1800 t/train；y=n*q=9000 t/h。只把 n 增加百分之十，y=9900 t/h。模型邊界：固定每列有效載重與發車率，不含尖峰到達或空車需求；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: n=5 trains/h, q=1800 t/train; y=n*q=9000 t/h. Increasing only n with a ten-percent increase gives y=9900 t/h. Boundary: Fixed useful payload and departure rate, excluding peak arrivals and empty returns; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以滿載率與實際發車間距區分模型與觀察，先用站場發車時間戳與貨物秤重帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use load factor and actual departure intervals to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n=5 trains/h, q=1800 t/train；y=n*q=9000 t/h。只把 n 增加百分之十，y=9900 t/h。模型邊界：固定每列有效載重與發車率，不含尖峰到達或空車需求；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: n=5 trains/h, q=1800 t/train; y=n*q=9000 t/h. Increasing only n with a ten-percent increase gives y=9900 t/h. Boundary: Fixed useful payload and departure rate, excluding peak arrivals and empty returns; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「列車單向運能」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Directional train throughput\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n=5 trains/h, q=1800 t/train；y=n*q=9000 t/h。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: n=5 trains/h, q=1800 t/train; y=n*q=9000 t/h."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n=5 trains/h, q=1800 t/train；y=n*q=9000 t/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: n=5 trains/h, q=1800 t/train; y=n*q=9000 t/h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b335-v16-03","title":"列車單向運能：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Directional train throughput: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「列車單向運能」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Directional train throughput” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以滿載率與實際發車間距區分模型與觀察，先用站場發車時間戳與貨物秤重帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「列車單向運能」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use load factor and actual departure intervals to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using yard departure timestamps and cargo weighing records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Directional train throughput. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「列車單向運能」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定每列有效載重與發車率，不含尖峰到達或空車需求如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量造成偏離的合成觀察，以滿載率與實際發車間距說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Directional train throughput, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Fixed useful payload and departure rate, excluding peak arrivals and empty returns. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow. Explain which evidence in load factor and actual departure intervals distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以滿載率與實際發車間距區分模型與觀察，先用站場發車時間戳與貨物秤重帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「列車單向運能」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use load factor and actual departure intervals to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using yard departure timestamps and cargo weighing records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Directional train throughput. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「列車單向運能」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定每列有效載重與發車率，不含尖峰到達或空車需求如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量造成偏離的合成觀察，以滿載率與實際發車間距說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Directional train throughput, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Fixed useful payload and departure rate, excluding peak arrivals and empty returns. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow. Explain which evidence in load factor and actual departure intervals distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「列車單向運能」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Directional train throughput\"?","options":["本單元以滿載率與實際發車間距區分模型與觀察，先用站場發車時間戳與貨物秤重帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞"],"optionsEn":["Use load factor and actual departure intervals to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以滿載率與實際發車間距區分模型與觀察，先用站場發車時間戳與貨物秤重帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use load factor and actual departure intervals to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b335-v16-04","title":"列車單向運能：失效診斷","titleEn":"Directional train throughput: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「列車單向運能」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Directional train throughput” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量。這個失效與「列車單向運能」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查滿載率與實際發車間距，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow. This failure and a measurement bias in Directional train throughput can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check load factor and actual departure intervals rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用滿載率與實際發車間距作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量。這個失效與「列車單向運能」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查滿載率與實際發車間距，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow. This failure and a measurement bias in Directional train throughput can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check load factor and actual departure intervals rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「列車單向運能」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Directional train throughput\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b335-v16-05","title":"坡道牽引分力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gradient traction force: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「坡道牽引分力」如何影響鹿特丹港貝圖威貨運線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gradient traction force” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Betuweroute freight railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"小坡度下重力沿軌分量與列車質量成正比，坡度正負號決定牽引或制動需求。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 215.82 kN。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。全列車處於同一小坡度，只計重力沿軌分量。使用坡度定位與車列總重作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「坡道牽引分力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"At small gradients the longitudinal gravitational force scales with train mass, and its sign distinguishes traction from braking demand. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 215.82 kN. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. The whole consist occupies one small gradient; only longitudinal gravity is included. Use gradient location and total consist mass as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gradient traction force” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=2000000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, s=0.01 1；y=m*g*s/1000=196.2 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=2000000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, s=0.01 1; y=m*g*s/1000=196.2 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「坡道牽引分力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gradient traction force”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-05-k1","title":"坡道牽引分力","titleEn":"Gradient traction force","text":"小坡度下重力沿軌分量與列車質量成正比，坡度正負號決定牽引或制動需求。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 215.82 kN。","textEn":"At small gradients the longitudinal gravitational force scales with train mass, and its sign distinguishes traction from braking demand. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「坡道牽引分力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gradient traction force\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界","小坡度下重力沿軌分量與列車質量成正比，坡度正負號決定牽引或制動需求。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary.","At small gradients the longitudinal gravitational force scales with train mass, and its sign distinguishes traction from braking demand."],"answer":2,"explanation":"小坡度下重力沿軌分量與列車質量成正比，坡度正負號決定牽引或制動需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"At small gradients the longitudinal gravitational force scales with train mass, and its sign distinguishes traction from braking demand. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b335-v16-06","title":"坡道牽引分力：定量估算","titleEn":"Gradient traction force: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「坡道牽引分力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gradient traction force” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=2000000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, s=0.01 1；y=m*g*s/1000=196.2 kN。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=215.82 kN。模型邊界：全列車處於同一小坡度，只計重力沿軌分量；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=2000000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, s=0.01 1; y=m*g*s/1000=196.2 kN. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=215.82 kN. Boundary: The whole consist occupies one small gradient; only longitudinal gravity is included; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以坡度定位與車列總重區分模型與觀察，先用合成坡度圖與逐車質量清單建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use gradient location and total consist mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=2000000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, s=0.01 1；y=m*g*s/1000=196.2 kN。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=215.82 kN。模型邊界：全列車處於同一小坡度，只計重力沿軌分量；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=2000000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, s=0.01 1; y=m*g*s/1000=196.2 kN. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=215.82 kN. Boundary: The whole consist occupies one small gradient; only longitudinal gravity is included; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「坡道牽引分力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gradient traction force\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=2000000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, s=0.01 1；y=m*g*s/1000=196.2 kN。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=2000000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, s=0.01 1; y=m*g*s/1000=196.2 kN.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=2000000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, s=0.01 1；y=m*g*s/1000=196.2 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=2000000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, s=0.01 1; y=m*g*s/1000=196.2 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b335-v16-07","title":"坡道牽引分力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gradient traction force: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「坡道牽引分力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gradient traction force” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以坡度定位與車列總重區分模型與觀察，先用合成坡度圖與逐車質量清單建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「坡道牽引分力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use gradient location and total consist mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic gradient profile and wagon mass list, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Gradient traction force. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「坡道牽引分力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出全列車處於同一小坡度，只計重力沿軌分量如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力造成偏離的合成觀察，以坡度定位與車列總重說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Gradient traction force, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: The whole consist occupies one small gradient; only longitudinal gravity is included. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force. Explain which evidence in gradient location and total consist mass distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以坡度定位與車列總重區分模型與觀察，先用合成坡度圖與逐車質量清單建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「坡道牽引分力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use gradient location and total consist mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic gradient profile and wagon mass list, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Gradient traction force. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「坡道牽引分力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出全列車處於同一小坡度，只計重力沿軌分量如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力造成偏離的合成觀察，以坡度定位與車列總重說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Gradient traction force, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: The whole consist occupies one small gradient; only longitudinal gravity is included. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force. Explain which evidence in gradient location and total consist mass distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「坡道牽引分力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gradient traction force\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以坡度定位與車列總重區分模型與觀察，先用合成坡度圖與逐車質量清單建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use gradient location and total consist mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以坡度定位與車列總重區分模型與觀察，先用合成坡度圖與逐車質量清單建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use gradient location and total consist mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b335-v16-08","title":"坡道牽引分力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gradient traction force: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「坡道牽引分力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gradient traction force” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力。這個失效與「坡道牽引分力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查坡度定位與車列總重，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force. This failure and a measurement bias in Gradient traction force can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check gradient location and total consist mass rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用坡度定位與車列總重作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力。這個失效與「坡道牽引分力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查坡度定位與車列總重，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force. This failure and a measurement bias in Gradient traction force can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check gradient location and total consist mass rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「坡道牽引分力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gradient traction force\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界","忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary.","Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force."],"answer":2,"explanation":"忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b335-v16-s2","title":"速度與牽引功率與貨列制動距離","titleEn":"Speed and tractive power & Freight braking distance","description":"本階段聚焦「速度與牽引功率」與「貨列制動距離」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Speed and tractive power\" and \"Freight braking distance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b335-v16-09","title":"速度與牽引功率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Speed and tractive power: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「速度與牽引功率」如何影響鹿特丹港貝圖威貨運線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Speed and tractive power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Betuweroute freight railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"同一牽引力在較高速度需要更高機械功率，功率限制與黏著限制是不同邊界。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 6.6 MW。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。輪周力與速度同時取得，只計機械功率。使用輪周功率與速度的同步紀錄作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「速度與牽引功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The same tractive force needs more mechanical power at higher speed; power and adhesion limits are different boundaries. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 6.6 MW. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Wheel force and speed are simultaneous; only mechanical power is counted. Use synchronous wheel-power and speed records as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Speed and tractive power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300000 N, v=20 m/s；y=F*v/1e6=6 MW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300000 N, v=20 m/s; y=F*v/1e6=6 MW.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「速度與牽引功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Speed and tractive power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-09-k1","title":"速度與牽引功率","titleEn":"Speed and tractive power","text":"同一牽引力在較高速度需要更高機械功率，功率限制與黏著限制是不同邊界。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 6.6 MW。","textEn":"The same tractive force needs more mechanical power at higher speed; power and adhesion limits are different boundaries. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「速度與牽引功率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Speed and tractive power\" is correct?","options":["同一牽引力在較高速度需要更高機械功率，功率限制與黏著限制是不同邊界。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離"],"optionsEn":["The same tractive force needs more mechanical power at higher speed; power and adhesion limits are different boundaries.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同一牽引力在較高速度需要更高機械功率，功率限制與黏著限制是不同邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The same tractive force needs more mechanical power at higher speed; power and adhesion limits are different boundaries. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b335-v16-10","title":"速度與牽引功率：定量估算","titleEn":"Speed and tractive power: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「速度與牽引功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Speed and tractive power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300000 N, v=20 m/s；y=F*v/1e6=6 MW。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=6.6 MW。模型邊界：輪周力與速度同時取得，只計機械功率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300000 N, v=20 m/s; y=F*v/1e6=6 MW. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=6.6 MW. Boundary: Wheel force and speed are simultaneous; only mechanical power is counted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以輪周功率與速度的同步紀錄區分模型與觀察，先用模擬輪周力與同步速度訊號建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use synchronous wheel-power and speed records to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300000 N, v=20 m/s；y=F*v/1e6=6 MW。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=6.6 MW。模型邊界：輪周力與速度同時取得，只計機械功率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300000 N, v=20 m/s; y=F*v/1e6=6 MW. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=6.6 MW. Boundary: Wheel force and speed are simultaneous; only mechanical power is counted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「速度與牽引功率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Speed and tractive power\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300000 N, v=20 m/s；y=F*v/1e6=6 MW。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300000 N, v=20 m/s; y=F*v/1e6=6 MW.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300000 N, v=20 m/s；y=F*v/1e6=6 MW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300000 N, v=20 m/s; y=F*v/1e6=6 MW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b335-v16-11","title":"速度與牽引功率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Speed and tractive power: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「速度與牽引功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Speed and tractive power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以輪周功率與速度的同步紀錄區分模型與觀察，先用模擬輪周力與同步速度訊號建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「速度與牽引功率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use synchronous wheel-power and speed records to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using simulated wheel force and synchronous speed signal, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Speed and tractive power. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「速度與牽引功率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出輪周力與速度同時取得，只計機械功率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界造成偏離的合成觀察，以輪周功率與速度的同步紀錄說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Speed and tractive power, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Wheel force and speed are simultaneous; only mechanical power is counted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary. Explain which evidence in synchronous wheel-power and speed records distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以輪周功率與速度的同步紀錄區分模型與觀察，先用模擬輪周力與同步速度訊號建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「速度與牽引功率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use synchronous wheel-power and speed records to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using simulated wheel force and synchronous speed signal, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Speed and tractive power. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「速度與牽引功率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出輪周力與速度同時取得，只計機械功率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界造成偏離的合成觀察，以輪周功率與速度的同步紀錄說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Speed and tractive power, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Wheel force and speed are simultaneous; only mechanical power is counted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary. Explain which evidence in synchronous wheel-power and speed records distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「速度與牽引功率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Speed and tractive power\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風","本單元以輪周功率與速度的同步紀錄區分模型與觀察，先用模擬輪周力與同步速度訊號建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation.","Use synchronous wheel-power and speed records to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以輪周功率與速度的同步紀錄區分模型與觀察，先用模擬輪周力與同步速度訊號建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use synchronous wheel-power and speed records to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b335-v16-12","title":"速度與牽引功率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Speed and tractive power: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「速度與牽引功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Speed and tractive power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界。這個失效與「速度與牽引功率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查輪周功率與速度的同步紀錄，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary. This failure and a measurement bias in Speed and tractive power can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check synchronous wheel-power and speed records rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用輪周功率與速度的同步紀錄作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界。這個失效與「速度與牽引功率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查輪周功率與速度的同步紀錄，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary. This failure and a measurement bias in Speed and tractive power can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check synchronous wheel-power and speed records rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「速度與牽引功率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Speed and tractive power\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離"],"optionsEn":["Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b335-v16-13","title":"貨列制動距離：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Freight braking distance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「貨列制動距離」如何影響鹿特丹港貝圖威貨運線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Freight braking distance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Betuweroute freight railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"制動建立前列車仍前進，反應距離與常減速度制動距離必須相加。本模型把 v 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 866.25 m。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。延遲時等速，其後固定減速度，不含坡度與黏著變化。使用制動建立延遲與速度衰減曲線作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「貨列制動距離」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The train continues moving while braking builds up, so delay distance must be added to constant-deceleration stopping distance. In this model, v is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 866.25 m. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Constant speed during delay followed by constant deceleration, without gradient or adhesion variation. Use brake build-up delay and speed-decay trace as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Freight braking distance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=25 m/s, a=0.5 m/s2, tau=4 s；y=v*tau+v**2/(2*a)=725 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=25 m/s, a=0.5 m/s2, tau=4 s; y=v*tau+v**2/(2*a)=725 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「貨列制動距離」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Freight braking distance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-13-k1","title":"貨列制動距離","titleEn":"Freight braking distance","text":"制動建立前列車仍前進，反應距離與常減速度制動距離必須相加。本模型把 v 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 866.25 m。","textEn":"The train continues moving while braking builds up, so delay distance must be added to constant-deceleration stopping distance. In this model, v is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「貨列制動距離」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Freight braking distance\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離","制動建立前列車仍前進，反應距離與常減速度制動距離必須相加。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance.","The train continues moving while braking builds up, so delay distance must be added to constant-deceleration stopping distance.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"制動建立前列車仍前進，反應距離與常減速度制動距離必須相加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The train continues moving while braking builds up, so delay distance must be added to constant-deceleration stopping distance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b335-v16-14","title":"貨列制動距離：定量估算","titleEn":"Freight braking distance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「貨列制動距離」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Freight braking distance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=25 m/s, a=0.5 m/s2, tau=4 s；y=v*tau+v**2/(2*a)=725 m。只把 v 增加百分之十，y=866.25 m。模型邊界：延遲時等速，其後固定減速度，不含坡度與黏著變化；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=25 m/s, a=0.5 m/s2, tau=4 s; y=v*tau+v**2/(2*a)=725 m. Increasing only v with a ten-percent increase gives y=866.25 m. Boundary: Constant speed during delay followed by constant deceleration, without gradient or adhesion variation; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以制動建立延遲與速度衰減曲線區分模型與觀察，先用合成制動命令、速度及減速度時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use brake build-up delay and speed-decay trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=25 m/s, a=0.5 m/s2, tau=4 s；y=v*tau+v**2/(2*a)=725 m。只把 v 增加百分之十，y=866.25 m。模型邊界：延遲時等速，其後固定減速度，不含坡度與黏著變化；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=25 m/s, a=0.5 m/s2, tau=4 s; y=v*tau+v**2/(2*a)=725 m. Increasing only v with a ten-percent increase gives y=866.25 m. Boundary: Constant speed during delay followed by constant deceleration, without gradient or adhesion variation; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「貨列制動距離」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Freight braking distance\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=25 m/s, a=0.5 m/s2, tau=4 s；y=v*tau+v**2/(2*a)=725 m。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=25 m/s, a=0.5 m/s2, tau=4 s; y=v*tau+v**2/(2*a)=725 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=25 m/s, a=0.5 m/s2, tau=4 s；y=v*tau+v**2/(2*a)=725 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=25 m/s, a=0.5 m/s2, tau=4 s; y=v*tau+v**2/(2*a)=725 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b335-v16-15","title":"貨列制動距離：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Freight braking distance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「貨列制動距離」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Freight braking distance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以制動建立延遲與速度衰減曲線區分模型與觀察，先用合成制動命令、速度及減速度時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「貨列制動距離」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use brake build-up delay and speed-decay trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic brake-command, speed and deceleration traces, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Freight braking distance. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「貨列制動距離」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出延遲時等速，其後固定減速度，不含坡度與黏著變化如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離造成偏離的合成觀察，以制動建立延遲與速度衰減曲線說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Freight braking distance, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Constant speed during delay followed by constant deceleration, without gradient or adhesion variation. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance. Explain which evidence in brake build-up delay and speed-decay trace distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以制動建立延遲與速度衰減曲線區分模型與觀察，先用合成制動命令、速度及減速度時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「貨列制動距離」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use brake build-up delay and speed-decay trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic brake-command, speed and deceleration traces, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Freight braking distance. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「貨列制動距離」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出延遲時等速，其後固定減速度，不含坡度與黏著變化如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離造成偏離的合成觀察，以制動建立延遲與速度衰減曲線說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Freight braking distance, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Constant speed during delay followed by constant deceleration, without gradient or adhesion variation. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance. Explain which evidence in brake build-up delay and speed-decay trace distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「貨列制動距離」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Freight braking distance\"?","options":["本單元以制動建立延遲與速度衰減曲線區分模型與觀察，先用合成制動命令、速度及減速度時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量"],"optionsEn":["Use brake build-up delay and speed-decay trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以制動建立延遲與速度衰減曲線區分模型與觀察，先用合成制動命令、速度及減速度時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use brake build-up delay and speed-decay trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b335-v16-16","title":"貨列制動距離：失效診斷","titleEn":"Freight braking distance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「貨列制動距離」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Freight braking distance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離。這個失效與「貨列制動距離」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查制動建立延遲與速度衰減曲線，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance. This failure and a measurement bias in Freight braking distance can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check brake build-up delay and speed-decay trace rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用制動建立延遲與速度衰減曲線作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離。這個失效與「貨列制動距離」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查制動建立延遲與速度衰減曲線，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance. This failure and a measurement bias in Freight braking distance can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check brake build-up delay and speed-decay trace rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「貨列制動距離」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Freight braking distance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b335-v16-s3","title":"貨物外廓餘量與閉塞占用時間","titleEn":"Cargo clearance margin & Block occupation time","description":"本階段聚焦「貨物外廓餘量」與「閉塞占用時間」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cargo clearance margin\" and \"Block occupation time\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b335-v16-17","title":"貨物外廓餘量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cargo clearance margin: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「貨物外廓餘量」如何影響鹿特丹港貝圖威貨運線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cargo clearance margin” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Betuweroute freight railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"靜態貨物高度之外仍須扣除動態擺動與測量不確定度，名義外廓不等於可用空間。本模型把 limit 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 550 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。同一垂向基準的標量包絡，不含側向外廓和不確定度餘量。使用貨物掃描與代表性搖擺包絡作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「貨物外廓餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dynamic movement and measurement uncertainty consume space beyond static cargo height; a nominal envelope is not usable clearance. In this model, limit is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 550 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Scalar vertical envelopes on one datum, excluding lateral envelopes and uncertainty reserve. Use cargo scans and representative sway envelopes as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cargo clearance margin” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：limit=4200 mm, load=4000 mm, sway=70 mm；y=limit-load-sway=130 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: limit=4200 mm, load=4000 mm, sway=70 mm; y=limit-load-sway=130 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「貨物外廓餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cargo clearance margin”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-17-k1","title":"貨物外廓餘量","titleEn":"Cargo clearance margin","text":"靜態貨物高度之外仍須扣除動態擺動與測量不確定度，名義外廓不等於可用空間。本模型把 limit 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 550 mm。","textEn":"Dynamic movement and measurement uncertainty consume space beyond static cargo height; a nominal envelope is not usable clearance. In this model, limit is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「貨物外廓餘量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cargo clearance margin\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用","靜態貨物高度之外仍須扣除動態擺動與測量不確定度，名義外廓不等於可用空間。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy.","Dynamic movement and measurement uncertainty consume space beyond static cargo height; a nominal envelope is not usable clearance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"靜態貨物高度之外仍須扣除動態擺動與測量不確定度，名義外廓不等於可用空間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dynamic movement and measurement uncertainty consume space beyond static cargo height; a nominal envelope is not usable clearance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b335-v16-18","title":"貨物外廓餘量：定量估算","titleEn":"Cargo clearance margin: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「貨物外廓餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cargo clearance margin” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：limit=4200 mm, load=4000 mm, sway=70 mm；y=limit-load-sway=130 mm。只把 limit 增加百分之十，y=550 mm。模型邊界：同一垂向基準的標量包絡，不含側向外廓和不確定度餘量；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: limit=4200 mm, load=4000 mm, sway=70 mm; y=limit-load-sway=130 mm. Increasing only limit with a ten-percent increase gives y=550 mm. Boundary: Scalar vertical envelopes on one datum, excluding lateral envelopes and uncertainty reserve; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以貨物掃描與代表性搖擺包絡區分模型與觀察，先用貨物輪廓掃描與動態外廓樣本建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use cargo scans and representative sway envelopes to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：limit=4200 mm, load=4000 mm, sway=70 mm；y=limit-load-sway=130 mm。只把 limit 增加百分之十，y=550 mm。模型邊界：同一垂向基準的標量包絡，不含側向外廓和不確定度餘量；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: limit=4200 mm, load=4000 mm, sway=70 mm; y=limit-load-sway=130 mm. Increasing only limit with a ten-percent increase gives y=550 mm. Boundary: Scalar vertical envelopes on one datum, excluding lateral envelopes and uncertainty reserve; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「貨物外廓餘量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cargo clearance margin\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：limit=4200 mm, load=4000 mm, sway=70 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: limit=4200 mm, load=4000 mm, sway=70 mm; y=limit-load-sway=130 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：limit=4200 mm, load=4000 mm, sway=70 mm；y=limit-load-sway=130 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: limit=4200 mm, load=4000 mm, sway=70 mm; y=limit-load-sway=130 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b335-v16-19","title":"貨物外廓餘量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cargo clearance margin: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「貨物外廓餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cargo clearance margin” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以貨物掃描與代表性搖擺包絡區分模型與觀察，先用貨物輪廓掃描與動態外廓樣本建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「貨物外廓餘量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use cargo scans and representative sway envelopes to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using cargo-profile scans and dynamic-envelope samples, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cargo clearance margin. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「貨物外廓餘量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出同一垂向基準的標量包絡，不含側向外廓和不確定度餘量如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造造成偏離的合成觀察，以貨物掃描與代表性搖擺包絡說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cargo clearance margin, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Scalar vertical envelopes on one datum, excluding lateral envelopes and uncertainty reserve. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures. Explain which evidence in cargo scans and representative sway envelopes distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以貨物掃描與代表性搖擺包絡區分模型與觀察，先用貨物輪廓掃描與動態外廓樣本建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「貨物外廓餘量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use cargo scans and representative sway envelopes to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using cargo-profile scans and dynamic-envelope samples, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cargo clearance margin. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「貨物外廓餘量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出同一垂向基準的標量包絡，不含側向外廓和不確定度餘量如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造造成偏離的合成觀察，以貨物掃描與代表性搖擺包絡說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cargo clearance margin, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Scalar vertical envelopes on one datum, excluding lateral envelopes and uncertainty reserve. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures. Explain which evidence in cargo scans and representative sway envelopes distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「貨物外廓餘量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cargo clearance margin\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以貨物掃描與代表性搖擺包絡區分模型與觀察，先用貨物輪廓掃描與動態外廓樣本建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use cargo scans and representative sway envelopes to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以貨物掃描與代表性搖擺包絡區分模型與觀察，先用貨物輪廓掃描與動態外廓樣本建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use cargo scans and representative sway envelopes to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b335-v16-20","title":"貨物外廓餘量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cargo clearance margin: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「貨物外廓餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cargo clearance margin” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造。這個失效與「貨物外廓餘量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查貨物掃描與代表性搖擺包絡，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures. This failure and a measurement bias in Cargo clearance margin can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check cargo scans and representative sway envelopes rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用貨物掃描與代表性搖擺包絡作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造。這個失效與「貨物外廓餘量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查貨物掃描與代表性搖擺包絡，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures. This failure and a measurement bias in Cargo clearance margin can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check cargo scans and representative sway envelopes rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「貨物外廓餘量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cargo clearance margin\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用","裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy.","Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b335-v16-21","title":"閉塞占用時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Block occupation time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「閉塞占用時間」如何影響鹿特丹港貝圖威貨運線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Block occupation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Betuweroute freight railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"路徑釋放取決於列車尾端離開受保護區，而非車頭通過訊號點。本模型把 L 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 112 s。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。固定速度、已知列車長度及固定解鎖裕量。使用頭尾通過時刻與解鎖狀態作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「閉塞占用時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A path is released when the rear clears the protected region, not merely when the front passes a signal. In this model, L is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 112 s. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Fixed speed, known train length and fixed release allowance. Use front and rear passing times with release status as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Block occupation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：L=1500 m, train=650 m, v=25 m/s, margin=20 s；y=(L+train)/v+margin=106 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: L=1500 m, train=650 m, v=25 m/s, margin=20 s; y=(L+train)/v+margin=106 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「閉塞占用時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Block occupation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-21-k1","title":"閉塞占用時間","titleEn":"Block occupation time","text":"路徑釋放取決於列車尾端離開受保護區，而非車頭通過訊號點。本模型把 L 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 112 s。","textEn":"A path is released when the rear clears the protected region, not merely when the front passes a signal. In this model, L is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閉塞占用時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Block occupation time\" is correct?","options":["路徑釋放取決於列車尾端離開受保護區，而非車頭通過訊號點。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離"],"optionsEn":["A path is released when the rear clears the protected region, not merely when the front passes a signal.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"路徑釋放取決於列車尾端離開受保護區，而非車頭通過訊號點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A path is released when the rear clears the protected region, not merely when the front passes a signal. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b335-v16-22","title":"閉塞占用時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Block occupation time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「閉塞占用時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Block occupation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：L=1500 m, train=650 m, v=25 m/s, margin=20 s；y=(L+train)/v+margin=106 s。只把 L 增加百分之十，y=112 s。模型邊界：固定速度、已知列車長度及固定解鎖裕量；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: L=1500 m, train=650 m, v=25 m/s, margin=20 s; y=(L+train)/v+margin=106 s. Increasing only L with a ten-percent increase gives y=112 s. Boundary: Fixed speed, known train length and fixed release allowance; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以頭尾通過時刻與解鎖狀態區分模型與觀察，先用合成車頭車尾通過時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use front and rear passing times with release status to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：L=1500 m, train=650 m, v=25 m/s, margin=20 s；y=(L+train)/v+margin=106 s。只把 L 增加百分之十，y=112 s。模型邊界：固定速度、已知列車長度及固定解鎖裕量；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: L=1500 m, train=650 m, v=25 m/s, margin=20 s; y=(L+train)/v+margin=106 s. Increasing only L with a ten-percent increase gives y=112 s. Boundary: Fixed speed, known train length and fixed release allowance; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「閉塞占用時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Block occupation time\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：L=1500 m, train=650 m, v=25 m/s, margin=20 s。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: L=1500 m, train=650 m, v=25 m/s, margin=20 s; y=(L+train)/v+margin=106 s.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：L=1500 m, train=650 m, v=25 m/s, margin=20 s；y=(L+train)/v+margin=106 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: L=1500 m, train=650 m, v=25 m/s, margin=20 s; y=(L+train)/v+margin=106 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b335-v16-23","title":"閉塞占用時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Block occupation time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「閉塞占用時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Block occupation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以頭尾通過時刻與解鎖狀態區分模型與觀察，先用合成車頭車尾通過時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「閉塞占用時間」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use front and rear passing times with release status to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic front and rear passage timestamps, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Block occupation time. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「閉塞占用時間」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定速度、已知列車長度及固定解鎖裕量如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用造成偏離的合成觀察，以頭尾通過時刻與解鎖狀態說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Block occupation time, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Fixed speed, known train length and fixed release allowance. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy. Explain which evidence in front and rear passing times with release status distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以頭尾通過時刻與解鎖狀態區分模型與觀察，先用合成車頭車尾通過時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「閉塞占用時間」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use front and rear passing times with release status to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic front and rear passage timestamps, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Block occupation time. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「閉塞占用時間」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定速度、已知列車長度及固定解鎖裕量如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用造成偏離的合成觀察，以頭尾通過時刻與解鎖狀態說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Block occupation time, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Fixed speed, known train length and fixed release allowance. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy. Explain which evidence in front and rear passing times with release status distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「閉塞占用時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Block occupation time\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界","本單元以頭尾通過時刻與解鎖狀態區分模型與觀察，先用合成車頭車尾通過時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary.","Use front and rear passing times with release status to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以頭尾通過時刻與解鎖狀態區分模型與觀察，先用合成車頭車尾通過時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use front and rear passing times with release status to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b335-v16-24","title":"閉塞占用時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Block occupation time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「閉塞占用時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Block occupation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用。這個失效與「閉塞占用時間」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查頭尾通過時刻與解鎖狀態，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy. This failure and a measurement bias in Block occupation time can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check front and rear passing times with release status rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用頭尾通過時刻與解鎖狀態作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用。這個失效與「閉塞占用時間」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查頭尾通過時刻與解鎖狀態，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy. This failure and a measurement bias in Block occupation time can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check front and rear passing times with release status rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「閉塞占用時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Block occupation time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b335-v16-s4","title":"滾動阻力能量與港區停留庫存","titleEn":"Rolling-resistance energy & Port dwell inventory","description":"本階段聚焦「滾動阻力能量」與「港區停留庫存」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rolling-resistance energy\" and \"Port dwell inventory\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b335-v16-25","title":"滾動阻力能量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rolling-resistance energy: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「滾動阻力能量」如何影響鹿特丹港貝圖威貨運線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rolling-resistance energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Betuweroute freight railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"阻力作功按距離積分，長距離低阻力仍可形成可觀耗能。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 122.222 kWh。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。固定阻力沿指定距離作功，不含加速或坡度能量。使用牽引能量與里程分段帳作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「滾動阻力能量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Resistance work is integrated over distance, so modest resistance over a long route can consume substantial energy. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 122.222 kWh. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Constant resistance over a stated distance, excluding acceleration and gradient energy. Use traction-energy accounts divided by route distance as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rolling-resistance energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=40000 N, L=10000 m；y=F*L/3.6e6=111.111 kWh。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=40000 N, L=10000 m; y=F*L/3.6e6=111.111 kWh.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「滾動阻力能量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rolling-resistance energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-25-k1","title":"滾動阻力能量","titleEn":"Rolling-resistance energy","text":"阻力作功按距離積分，長距離低阻力仍可形成可觀耗能。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 122.222 kWh。","textEn":"Resistance work is integrated over distance, so modest resistance over a long route can consume substantial energy. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「滾動阻力能量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rolling-resistance energy\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離","阻力作功按距離積分，長距離低阻力仍可形成可觀耗能。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance.","Resistance work is integrated over distance, so modest resistance over a long route can consume substantial energy.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory."],"answer":1,"explanation":"阻力作功按距離積分，長距離低阻力仍可形成可觀耗能。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Resistance work is integrated over distance, so modest resistance over a long route can consume substantial energy. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b335-v16-26","title":"滾動阻力能量：定量估算","titleEn":"Rolling-resistance energy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「滾動阻力能量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rolling-resistance energy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=40000 N, L=10000 m；y=F*L/3.6e6=111.111 kWh。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=122.222 kWh。模型邊界：固定阻力沿指定距離作功，不含加速或坡度能量；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=40000 N, L=10000 m; y=F*L/3.6e6=111.111 kWh. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=122.222 kWh. Boundary: Constant resistance over a stated distance, excluding acceleration and gradient energy; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以牽引能量與里程分段帳區分模型與觀察，先用模型牽引力計與里程積分紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use traction-energy accounts divided by route distance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=40000 N, L=10000 m；y=F*L/3.6e6=111.111 kWh。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=122.222 kWh。模型邊界：固定阻力沿指定距離作功，不含加速或坡度能量；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=40000 N, L=10000 m; y=F*L/3.6e6=111.111 kWh. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=122.222 kWh. Boundary: Constant resistance over a stated distance, excluding acceleration and gradient energy; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「滾動阻力能量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rolling-resistance energy\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=40000 N, L=10000 m；y=F*L/3.6e6=111.111 kWh。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=40000 N, L=10000 m; y=F*L/3.6e6=111.111 kWh."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=40000 N, L=10000 m；y=F*L/3.6e6=111.111 kWh。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=40000 N, L=10000 m; y=F*L/3.6e6=111.111 kWh. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b335-v16-27","title":"滾動阻力能量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rolling-resistance energy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「滾動阻力能量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rolling-resistance energy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以牽引能量與里程分段帳區分模型與觀察，先用模型牽引力計與里程積分紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「滾動阻力能量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use traction-energy accounts divided by route distance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model force gauge and distance integration record, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Rolling-resistance energy. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「滾動阻力能量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定阻力沿指定距離作功，不含加速或坡度能量如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離造成偏離的合成觀察，以牽引能量與里程分段帳說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Rolling-resistance energy, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Constant resistance over a stated distance, excluding acceleration and gradient energy. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance. Explain which evidence in traction-energy accounts divided by route distance distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以牽引能量與里程分段帳區分模型與觀察，先用模型牽引力計與里程積分紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「滾動阻力能量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use traction-energy accounts divided by route distance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model force gauge and distance integration record, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Rolling-resistance energy. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「滾動阻力能量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定阻力沿指定距離作功，不含加速或坡度能量如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離造成偏離的合成觀察，以牽引能量與里程分段帳說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Rolling-resistance energy, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Constant resistance over a stated distance, excluding acceleration and gradient energy. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance. Explain which evidence in traction-energy accounts divided by route distance distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「滾動阻力能量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rolling-resistance energy\"?","options":["本單元以牽引能量與里程分段帳區分模型與觀察，先用模型牽引力計與里程積分紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離"],"optionsEn":["Use traction-energy accounts divided by route distance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以牽引能量與里程分段帳區分模型與觀察，先用模型牽引力計與里程積分紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use traction-energy accounts divided by route distance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b335-v16-28","title":"滾動阻力能量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rolling-resistance energy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「滾動阻力能量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rolling-resistance energy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離。這個失效與「滾動阻力能量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查牽引能量與里程分段帳，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance. This failure and a measurement bias in Rolling-resistance energy can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check traction-energy accounts divided by route distance rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用牽引能量與里程分段帳作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離。這個失效與「滾動阻力能量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查牽引能量與里程分段帳，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance. This failure and a measurement bias in Rolling-resistance energy can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check traction-energy accounts divided by route distance rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「滾動阻力能量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rolling-resistance energy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b335-v16-29","title":"港區停留庫存：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Port dwell inventory: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「港區停留庫存」如何影響鹿特丹港貝圖威貨運線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Port dwell inventory” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Betuweroute freight railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"穩態到達率乘平均停留時間給出平均在場列車數，但不提供尖峰排隊的上界。本模型把 lam 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 11 trains。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。穩態平均到達率且無持續積累，不預測尖峰隊長。使用到達時刻、離開時刻與在場列車數作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「港區停留庫存」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Arrival rate times average dwell gives mean inventory in steady conditions, but does not bound peak queues. In this model, lam is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 11 trains. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Steady mean arrival rate without growing inventory; peak queues are not predicted. Use arrival times, departure times and yard inventory as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Port dwell inventory” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lam=4 trains/h, T=2.5 h；y=lam*T=10 trains。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: lam=4 trains/h, T=2.5 h; y=lam*T=10 trains.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「港區停留庫存」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Port dwell inventory”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-29-k1","title":"港區停留庫存","titleEn":"Port dwell inventory","text":"穩態到達率乘平均停留時間給出平均在場列車數，但不提供尖峰排隊的上界。本模型把 lam 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 11 trains。","textEn":"Arrival rate times average dwell gives mean inventory in steady conditions, but does not bound peak queues. In this model, lam is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「港區停留庫存」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Port dwell inventory\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音","穩態到達率乘平均停留時間給出平均在場列車數，但不提供尖峰排隊的上界。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy.","Arrival rate times average dwell gives mean inventory in steady conditions, but does not bound peak queues."],"answer":2,"explanation":"穩態到達率乘平均停留時間給出平均在場列車數，但不提供尖峰排隊的上界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Arrival rate times average dwell gives mean inventory in steady conditions, but does not bound peak queues. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b335-v16-30","title":"港區停留庫存：定量估算","titleEn":"Port dwell inventory: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「港區停留庫存」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Port dwell inventory” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lam=4 trains/h, T=2.5 h；y=lam*T=10 trains。只把 lam 增加百分之十，y=11 trains。模型邊界：穩態平均到達率且無持續積累，不預測尖峰隊長；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: lam=4 trains/h, T=2.5 h; y=lam*T=10 trains. Increasing only lam with a ten-percent increase gives y=11 trains. Boundary: Steady mean arrival rate without growing inventory; peak queues are not predicted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以到達時刻、離開時刻與在場列車數區分模型與觀察，先用進出站場事件紀錄與在場盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use arrival times, departure times and yard inventory to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lam=4 trains/h, T=2.5 h；y=lam*T=10 trains。只把 lam 增加百分之十，y=11 trains。模型邊界：穩態平均到達率且無持續積累，不預測尖峰隊長；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: lam=4 trains/h, T=2.5 h; y=lam*T=10 trains. Increasing only lam with a ten-percent increase gives y=11 trains. Boundary: Steady mean arrival rate without growing inventory; peak queues are not predicted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「港區停留庫存」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Port dwell inventory\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lam=4 trains/h, T=2.5 h；y=lam*T=10 trains。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: lam=4 trains/h, T=2.5 h; y=lam*T=10 trains.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lam=4 trains/h, T=2.5 h；y=lam*T=10 trains。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: lam=4 trains/h, T=2.5 h; y=lam*T=10 trains. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b335-v16-31","title":"港區停留庫存：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Port dwell inventory: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「港區停留庫存」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Port dwell inventory” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以到達時刻、離開時刻與在場列車數區分模型與觀察，先用進出站場事件紀錄與在場盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「港區停留庫存」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use arrival times, departure times and yard inventory to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using yard entry-exit event records and inventory counts, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Port dwell inventory. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「港區停留庫存」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出穩態平均到達率且無持續積累，不預測尖峰隊長如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞造成偏離的合成觀察，以到達時刻、離開時刻與在場列車數說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Port dwell inventory, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Steady mean arrival rate without growing inventory; peak queues are not predicted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory. Explain which evidence in arrival times, departure times and yard inventory distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以到達時刻、離開時刻與在場列車數區分模型與觀察，先用進出站場事件紀錄與在場盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「港區停留庫存」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use arrival times, departure times and yard inventory to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using yard entry-exit event records and inventory counts, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Port dwell inventory. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「港區停留庫存」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出穩態平均到達率且無持續積累，不預測尖峰隊長如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞造成偏離的合成觀察，以到達時刻、離開時刻與在場列車數說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Port dwell inventory, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Steady mean arrival rate without growing inventory; peak queues are not predicted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory. Explain which evidence in arrival times, departure times and yard inventory distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「港區停留庫存」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Port dwell inventory\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以到達時刻、離開時刻與在場列車數區分模型與觀察，先用進出站場事件紀錄與在場盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use arrival times, departure times and yard inventory to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以到達時刻、離開時刻與在場列車數區分模型與觀察，先用進出站場事件紀錄與在場盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use arrival times, departure times and yard inventory to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b335-v16-32","title":"港區停留庫存：失效診斷","titleEn":"Port dwell inventory: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「港區停留庫存」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Port dwell inventory” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞。這個失效與「港區停留庫存」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查到達時刻、離開時刻與在場列車數，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory. This failure and a measurement bias in Port dwell inventory can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check arrival times, departure times and yard inventory rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用到達時刻、離開時刻與在場列車數作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞。這個失效與「港區停留庫存」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查到達時刻、離開時刻與在場列車數，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory. This failure and a measurement bias in Port dwell inventory can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check arrival times, departure times and yard inventory rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「港區停留庫存」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Port dwell inventory\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音","到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy.","Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory."],"answer":2,"explanation":"到達成群時平均庫存可能掩蓋短時壅塞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Bunched arrivals can hide short congestion behind a moderate average inventory. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b335-v16-s5","title":"列車噪音能量比較與隧道換氣量級","titleEn":"Train noise-energy comparison & Tunnel ventilation scale","description":"本階段聚焦「列車噪音能量比較」與「隧道換氣量級」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Train noise-energy comparison\" and \"Tunnel ventilation scale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b335-v16-33","title":"列車噪音能量比較：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Train noise-energy comparison: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「列車噪音能量比較」如何影響鹿特丹港貝圖威貨運線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Train noise-energy comparison” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Betuweroute freight railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"同聲能事件數倍增只改變能量總量，不代表單一列車更吵。本模型把 n 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加一個整數單位，輸出增加為 3.35792 dB。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。各事件聲暴露相同且能量相加，不含不同列車差異。使用相同距離的事件聲暴露與事件數作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「列車噪音能量比較」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Multiplying equal-energy events increases total energy without making an individual train louder. In this model, n is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. An increase of one whole unit means the output increases to 3.35792 dB. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Equal sound exposure per event with additive energy, excluding differences among trains. Use event sound exposure and count at equal distance as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Train noise-energy comparison” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n=12 events, ref=6 events；y=10*log(n/ref)/log(10)=3.0103 dB。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: n=12 events, ref=6 events; y=10*log(n/ref)/log(10)=3.0103 dB.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「列車噪音能量比較」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Train noise-energy comparison”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-33-k1","title":"列車噪音能量比較","titleEn":"Train noise-energy comparison","text":"同聲能事件數倍增只改變能量總量，不代表單一列車更吵。本模型把 n 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加一個整數單位，輸出增加為 3.35792 dB。","textEn":"Multiplying equal-energy events increases total energy without making an individual train louder. In this model, n is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「列車噪音能量比較」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Train noise-energy comparison\" is correct?","options":["同聲能事件數倍增只改變能量總量，不代表單一列車更吵。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風"],"optionsEn":["Multiplying equal-energy events increases total energy without making an individual train louder.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同聲能事件數倍增只改變能量總量，不代表單一列車更吵。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Multiplying equal-energy events increases total energy without making an individual train louder. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b335-v16-34","title":"列車噪音能量比較：定量估算","titleEn":"Train noise-energy comparison: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「列車噪音能量比較」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Train noise-energy comparison” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n=12 events, ref=6 events；y=10*log(n/ref)/log(10)=3.0103 dB。只把 n 增加一個整數單位，y=3.35792 dB。模型邊界：各事件聲暴露相同且能量相加，不含不同列車差異；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: n=12 events, ref=6 events; y=10*log(n/ref)/log(10)=3.0103 dB. Increasing only n with an increase of one whole unit gives y=3.35792 dB. Boundary: Equal sound exposure per event with additive energy, excluding differences among trains; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以相同距離的事件聲暴露與事件數區分模型與觀察，先用固定位置聲暴露計與事件計數建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use event sound exposure and count at equal distance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n=12 events, ref=6 events；y=10*log(n/ref)/log(10)=3.0103 dB。只把 n 增加一個整數單位，y=3.35792 dB。模型邊界：各事件聲暴露相同且能量相加，不含不同列車差異；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: n=12 events, ref=6 events; y=10*log(n/ref)/log(10)=3.0103 dB. Increasing only n with an increase of one whole unit gives y=3.35792 dB. Boundary: Equal sound exposure per event with additive energy, excluding differences among trains; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「列車噪音能量比較」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Train noise-energy comparison\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略尾車仍在另一坡段會誤算整列車受力","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n=12 events, ref=6 events；y=10*log(n/ref)/log(10)=3.0103 dB。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計算穩態制動段會低估長車列停車距離"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring wagons still on another gradient miscalculates total force.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: n=12 events, ref=6 events; y=10*log(n/ref)/log(10)=3.0103 dB.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only steady braking underestimates a long consist stopping distance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n=12 events, ref=6 events；y=10*log(n/ref)/log(10)=3.0103 dB。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: n=12 events, ref=6 events; y=10*log(n/ref)/log(10)=3.0103 dB. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b335-v16-35","title":"列車噪音能量比較：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Train noise-energy comparison: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「列車噪音能量比較」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Train noise-energy comparison” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以相同距離的事件聲暴露與事件數區分模型與觀察，先用固定位置聲暴露計與事件計數建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「列車噪音能量比較」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use event sound exposure and count at equal distance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using fixed-position sound-exposure meter and event counter, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Train noise-energy comparison. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「列車噪音能量比較」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出各事件聲暴露相同且能量相加，不含不同列車差異如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音造成偏離的合成觀察，以相同距離的事件聲暴露與事件數說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Train noise-energy comparison, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Equal sound exposure per event with additive energy, excluding differences among trains. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy. Explain which evidence in event sound exposure and count at equal distance distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以相同距離的事件聲暴露與事件數區分模型與觀察，先用固定位置聲暴露計與事件計數建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「列車噪音能量比較」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use event sound exposure and count at equal distance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using fixed-position sound-exposure meter and event counter, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Train noise-energy comparison. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「列車噪音能量比較」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出各事件聲暴露相同且能量相加，不含不同列車差異如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音造成偏離的合成觀察，以相同距離的事件聲暴露與事件數說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Train noise-energy comparison, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Equal sound exposure per event with additive energy, excluding differences among trains. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy. Explain which evidence in event sound exposure and count at equal distance distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「列車噪音能量比較」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Train noise-energy comparison\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略列車長度會讓理論班距低於實際占用","本單元以相同距離的事件聲暴露與事件數區分模型與觀察，先用固定位置聲暴露計與事件計數建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring train length produces a theoretical headway below real occupancy.","Use event sound exposure and count at equal distance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以相同距離的事件聲暴露與事件數區分模型與觀察，先用固定位置聲暴露計與事件計數建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use event sound exposure and count at equal distance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b335-v16-36","title":"列車噪音能量比較：失效診斷","titleEn":"Train noise-energy comparison: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「列車噪音能量比較」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Train noise-energy comparison” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音。這個失效與「列車噪音能量比較」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查相同距離的事件聲暴露與事件數，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy. This failure and a measurement bias in Train noise-energy comparison can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check event sound exposure and count at equal distance rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用相同距離的事件聲暴露與事件數作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音。這個失效與「列車噪音能量比較」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查相同距離的事件聲暴露與事件數，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy. This failure and a measurement bias in Train noise-energy comparison can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check event sound exposure and count at equal distance rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「列車噪音能量比較」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Train noise-energy comparison\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風"],"optionsEn":["Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將分貝直接相加會嚴重誤判累積噪音。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adding decibels directly misrepresents accumulated sound energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b335-v16-37","title":"隧道換氣量級：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tunnel ventilation scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「隧道換氣量級」如何影響鹿特丹港貝圖威貨運線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tunnel ventilation scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Betuweroute freight railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平均流速乘有效斷面給出體積流量，列車活塞作用與局部回流需另列。本模型把 A 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 85.8 m3/s。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。有效斷面上的均勻平均風速，不含暫態活塞效應。使用多點風速與有效斷面作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「隧道換氣量級」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mean velocity times effective area gives volume flow, while piston action and local recirculation need separate treatment. In this model, A is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 85.8 m3/s. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniform mean velocity across effective area, excluding transient piston effects. Use multi-point air velocity and effective area as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tunnel ventilation scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：A=65 m2, u=1.2 m/s；y=A*u=78 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: A=65 m2, u=1.2 m/s; y=A*u=78 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「隧道換氣量級」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tunnel ventilation scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-37-k1","title":"隧道換氣量級","titleEn":"Tunnel ventilation scale","text":"平均流速乘有效斷面給出體積流量，列車活塞作用與局部回流需另列。本模型把 A 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 85.8 m3/s。","textEn":"Mean velocity times effective area gives volume flow, while piston action and local recirculation need separate treatment. In this model, A is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「隧道換氣量級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tunnel ventilation scale\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風","平均流速乘有效斷面給出體積流量，列車活塞作用與局部回流需另列。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation.","Mean velocity times effective area gives volume flow, while piston action and local recirculation need separate treatment.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均流速乘有效斷面給出體積流量，列車活塞作用與局部回流需另列。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mean velocity times effective area gives volume flow, while piston action and local recirculation need separate treatment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b335-v16-38","title":"隧道換氣量級：定量估算","titleEn":"Tunnel ventilation scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隧道換氣量級」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tunnel ventilation scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：A=65 m2, u=1.2 m/s；y=A*u=78 m3/s。只把 A 增加百分之十，y=85.8 m3/s。模型邊界：有效斷面上的均勻平均風速，不含暫態活塞效應；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: A=65 m2, u=1.2 m/s; y=A*u=78 m3/s. Increasing only A with a ten-percent increase gives y=85.8 m3/s. Boundary: Uniform mean velocity across effective area, excluding transient piston effects; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以多點風速與有效斷面區分模型與觀察，先用多點風速計與斷面量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use multi-point air velocity and effective area to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：A=65 m2, u=1.2 m/s；y=A*u=78 m3/s。只把 A 增加百分之十，y=85.8 m3/s。模型邊界：有效斷面上的均勻平均風速，不含暫態活塞效應；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: A=65 m2, u=1.2 m/s; y=A*u=78 m3/s. Increasing only A with a ten-percent increase gives y=85.8 m3/s. Boundary: Uniform mean velocity across effective area, excluding transient piston effects; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「隧道換氣量級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tunnel ventilation scale\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把低速最大牽引力延用到高速會超出功率邊界","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：裝載偏心會使動態外廓侵入鄰近構造","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：A=65 m2, u=1.2 m/s；y=A*u=78 m3/s。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending maximum low-speed force to high speed exceeds the power boundary.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Eccentric loading can move the dynamic envelope into nearby structures.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: A=65 m2, u=1.2 m/s; y=A*u=78 m3/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：A=65 m2, u=1.2 m/s；y=A*u=78 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: A=65 m2, u=1.2 m/s; y=A*u=78 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b335-v16-39","title":"隧道換氣量級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tunnel ventilation scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隧道換氣量級」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tunnel ventilation scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以多點風速與有效斷面區分模型與觀察，先用多點風速計與斷面量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「隧道換氣量級」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use multi-point air velocity and effective area to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using multi-point anemometers and section measurements, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Tunnel ventilation scale. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「隧道換氣量級」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出有效斷面上的均勻平均風速，不含暫態活塞效應如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風造成偏離的合成觀察，以多點風速與有效斷面說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Tunnel ventilation scale, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform mean velocity across effective area, excluding transient piston effects. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation. Explain which evidence in multi-point air velocity and effective area distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以多點風速與有效斷面區分模型與觀察，先用多點風速計與斷面量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「隧道換氣量級」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use multi-point air velocity and effective area to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using multi-point anemometers and section measurements, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Tunnel ventilation scale. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「隧道換氣量級」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出有效斷面上的均勻平均風速，不含暫態活塞效應如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風造成偏離的合成觀察，以多點風速與有效斷面說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Tunnel ventilation scale, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform mean velocity across effective area, excluding transient piston effects. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation. Explain which evidence in multi-point air velocity and effective area distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「隧道換氣量級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tunnel ventilation scale\"?","options":["本單元以多點風速與有效斷面區分模型與觀察，先用多點風速計與斷面量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用單次瞬時功率代表整段能量會混淆時間與距離"],"optionsEn":["Use multi-point air velocity and effective area to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using one instantaneous power value confuses energy with time and distance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以多點風速與有效斷面區分模型與觀察，先用多點風速計與斷面量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use multi-point air velocity and effective area to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b335-v16-40","title":"隧道換氣量級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tunnel ventilation scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"prerequisiteIds":["b335-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隧道換氣量級」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tunnel ventilation scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風。這個失效與「隧道換氣量級」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查多點風速與有效斷面，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation. This failure and a measurement bias in Tunnel ventilation scale can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check multi-point air velocity and effective area rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用多點風速與有效斷面作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b335-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風。這個失效與「隧道換氣量級」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查多點風速與有效斷面，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation. This failure and a measurement bias in Tunnel ventilation scale can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check multi-point air velocity and effective area rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]},{"id":"b335-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「隧道換氣量級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tunnel ventilation scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把額定載重當實際載重會高估貨物流量"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using rated payload as actual payload overstates cargo flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只用中心風速代表全斷面會高估或低估通風。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using only centreline velocity misrepresents total ventilation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-betuwe-history","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-brake"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b335-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b335-en.svg"}};
